From: Kevin Cahalan <kevinacahalan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: k3: reset a C66x that acknowledged shutdown

k3_rproc_stop() sends RP_MBOX_SHUTDOWN, waits for the ACK, and then for
the core to report WFI before it resets the core. On the BeagleBone AI-64
(J721E), a C66x that has sent the ACK and executed IDLE never reports
WFI, so the stop fails with -ETIMEDOUT and the core cannot be restarted.

A core with a local reset (uses_lreset, the C66x) is safe to hold in
reset once it has acknowledged, so do that when WFI does not show up.
The C7x, which has no local reset, still has to report WFI.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific workaround]
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c
@@ -386,7 +386,11 @@
 	};
 
 	ret = readx_poll_timeout(is_core_in_wfi, kproc, stat, stat, 200, 2000);
-	if (ret)
+	/*
+	 * A C66x never reports WFI, even when it has acknowledged and is
+	 * idle. A core with a local reset is safe to reset anyway.
+	 */
+	if (ret && !kproc->data->uses_lreset)
 		return ret;
 
 	return k3_rproc_reset(kproc);
